\[
\frac{1}{f_2} \approx 0.2505 \quad \Rightarrow \quad f_2 \approx 3.99 \, \text{cm}
\]

Using \( f_1 = -1.6624 f_2 \):  
\[
f_1 = -1.6624 \cdot 3.99 \approx -6.63 \, \text{cm}
\]

Thus, the focal lengths are \( f_2 = 3.99 \, \text{cm} \) and \( f_1 = -6.63 \, \text{cm} \), which matches **option I**.

